# CODEOWNERS
#
# Owner: @davinakmalyasha
#
# A CODEOWNERS file whose only reviewer is the author of the change is
# decoration. GitHub will happily show "1 approval required" on a pull request
# whose reviewer has written the diff, and nothing in the UI distinguishes
# that from review by somebody else. So this file is not a control, and it is
# worth being explicit about that rather than letting a reviewer assume
# otherwise.
#
# Review here is currently self-review. It is still worth doing: the checks in
# CONTRIBUTING.md — schema drift, the error-status meta-test, the realtime
# contract test — are written to fail on a mistake the author did not notice,
# which is most of them. What self-review cannot do is catch a wrong
# assumption held confidently, and on the clinical paths that is the real
# limitation of this repository.
#
# The value of listing the paths below is that it says which files are
# load-bearing, and where a reviewer should be slowest. It becomes a real
# control the moment a second person has write access.

# Default owner for everything not matched more specifically.
*                               @davinakmalyasha

